ed red also signifies danger  and it's only fitting that his  neighbor's name happens to be red the  walls of her apartment are even painted  all red and they both live on the 7th  floor which if you're going by Dante's 7  circles of hell  number seven is violence later on in the  film the red lights  become more apparent here in the bar the  backyard of Melanie's behind him in his  own apartment the red hallway the tree  market and finally in the background  when Melanie utters the line look at all  the pretty lights before the crash blue  is equal parts as important but doesn't  show up as frequently blue signifies  happiness and is more evident early on  especially when Wilson is courting  Melanie Winnie jerks off as puka his  eyes are blue but is surrounded by  smaller red lights that of passion but  as we continue the story we find Wilson  down on his luck he's a struggling actor  having newly moved to the city and is  desperately alone but that's all about  to change with the introduction of puka  Wilson recites lines for Charles  Dickens's A Christmas Carol for an  upcoming audition in essence puka is a  modern twist on this story about a man  who has serious shortcomings like a  Christmas carols Ebenezer Scrooge but by  seeing what he's caused and what will  happen to him he changes for the better  this story is told by using the past  present and future just like how a  beanie zur was visited by the ghosts of  Christmas past present and future  Wilson's past whoever involves meeting  Melanie at the open house you can even  tell by the date here October that it's  not even close to Christmas when he  first meets her he talks about how he'd  furnished the room with a big leather  chair and abstract art and guess what  when we see him in the present his home  has been adorned with a leather chair  and abstract art Wilson does get his job  as puka and it takes off allowing him  enough money to eventually buy his home  and move in with Melanie and tie we know  he was likely very successful as an  actor judging by this photo here of him  on the red carpet this success whoever  got to his head in and became more and  more temperamental which we also see in  the film as he gets increasingly angry  toward Melanie eventually culminating in  him slapping a boy at Ty's birthday  party for making fun of his son Melanie  asked him to leave and he does but comes  crawling back asking for a second chance  and this is where we get into the  present this is the moment where  everything can change when Melanie  either decides to take Wilson Mack or  not  Wilson even tells her not to listen to  alternate Wilson because he's learned  how terrible he is and this is also the  key moment in Wilson's journey as our  protein  honest he's learned the error of his  ways by going through this journey and  does not want to become what the future  might hold  just like how Scrooge decides to change  after seeing what will happen to him  but with Wilson he has a literal killing  of the old self in the scene where he  chops the burning puka with an axe it is  the physical representation of him  killing his old self  an old self that let fame success in his  anger get the best of him it's only by  killing this part of him can he see the  error of his ways become a new man and  changed the future so it's no surprise  that when Wilson sees the confrontation  between Melanie and alternate Wilson  he tells Melanie not to trust him but  she does anyway and this is important  because Wilson's journey isn't  completely over he must confront the  worst thing that could possibly happen  to him his heart of darkness and he'll  see this in his future the death of his  wife and child  this is the final moment where he'll  truly learn that family is more  important than money or fame Puka our  Christmas Carol ghost here is like the  ghost of Christmas future showing him  the future standing by his side and just  like in Dickens Tale he doesn't speak  and perhaps the reason both pukka and  the ghost of Christmas future don't  speak is to show how Wilson has the  freewill to change the future while the  past can't be changed and the present is  occurring the future is still unknown it  is yet to be written  this is also a good time to mention that  puka is derived from the Irish word puka  for spirit or ghost it's a creature from  Celtic folklore considered to be the  bringer of both good or bad fortune they  could take the shape of animals such as  a hare and in our case it looks just  like that with a pretty big exception  the eyes and mouth resembled that of a  front car hinting at the eventual car  crash but let's take a moment to discuss  read the driver of the other vehicle  this crash wasn't just Wilson's fault  for speeding notice here the speed limit  of 35 but it was also Reds alcoholism if  you remember when the detective finds  red having jumped from the apartment he  calls it a suicide that it was the  bottle that got to her and even in the  first scene where red welcomes Wilson  into his apartment early in the morning  she asks him if he wants a drink more  tragic are the pictures of her and her  daughter on the mantle the daughter she  herself killed in the accident she even  says  she feared being alone for Christmas  until Wilson arrived remember though  that all these memories are jumbled and  some are out of place and don't make  sense that's the point look how the  pooka producer is also a paramedic  Wilson meets at the end and there's no  better indication of this than the guy  I'll simply refer to as the family man  now this is easy to miss but also quite  interesting in the beginning of the film  at the coffee shop Wilson has asked if  he could take a picture for this family  take a look at this guy here it's the  same guy who Wilson will later ask to  take a picture with his family but it  doesn't stop there  guess who's interviewed about the pooka  recalls the family man and who beats up  Wilson on the street later same guy he  also asks if there was a struggle  outside the apartment where red  committed suicide and now I'm not a  hundred percent sure on this one since I  couldn't get a good look but he could  also be the other paramedic at the end  here Wilson's mind is a jumbled mess  where some things are remembered and  some things aren't just like how the  producer said the pooka doll decides  what things are remembered and what  aren't that's why the timeline in this  film is tough to follow and sometimes  doesn't make any sense but behind all  this mystery and what some may find an  ambiguous ending I found a beautiful  story about one man's acknowledgement of  the past to change himself for the  better I hope you enjoyed this ending  explained video please make sure to LIKE  subscribe and share I make a ton of  different types of videos like this and  I hope you'll check it out and I'll be  coming out with more in the future for  all my fans who know how I like to end  my videos remember daddy loves you very  much

